A||||1||DH||Slipping Clutch
Z||000000||DH||04-06-99||09:36 PM||||I've got an 88 GT, just like the one above, with 20,000 miles. My problem is that after about 50 miles the clutch will slip slightly. It's noticable when the speed control is on and you are climbing. It will not slip when you first start off.  I have never spun the wheels and drive it very easy.  
Z||000001||theogre||04-06-99||10:25 PM||||plan on pulling the tranny, but check the slave cyl first. it might be binding which would keep the throw out bearing excesivly loaded, and as things warm up it could be pressing on the fork enough to partly release the clutch.<p>I'd say at this point tho you probly have a burnt clutch and it should be replaced along with anything else that needs it. Get the flywheel cut(resurfaced) while your at it.
